Ported parts. Each file names its source and its changes in its header.

- crates/quota-station-core/src/quota/mod.rs
  from src/types.ts, src/lib/time.ts and src/providers/common.ts: the
  reading model (window ids, state words), percent used rounded and
  clamped, percent left, and a failed read served as stale.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/quota/cache.rs
  from src/cache.ts and src/providers/common.ts: when the last reading
  answers instead of a new read, which of its windows may stand in as
  stale, and forgetting it on a confirmed sign-out.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/quota/codex.rs
  from src/providers/codex.ts: the login read from auth.json, the two
  usage endpoints, the errors and the windows.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/quota/agy.rs
  from src/providers/agy.ts: agy -p /quota with a guard against opening a
  browser, then the local language server found with ps and lsof, the
  group and bucket names and the time limits.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/quota/claude.rs (its read of Claude Code's
  login)
  from src/providers/claude.ts: the login from the Keychain item, then
  .credentials.json, the usage endpoint and its header, the windows, and
  how a 401, a 429 and an unreadable Keychain are told.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/quota/semantics.rs
  from src/interpretation.ts: which windows bound which scope, the
  effective percent and the limiting windows.

What was changed:

- No login is ever refreshed, rotated or written: no token endpoint, no
  Codex app-server, no Pi or environment logins, no other profiles.
- No email, account id or plan is kept: an Antigravity account is told by
  a hash of its email, and the cache holds only windows, times and a hash
  of the login it was read with.
- The Keychain prompt is the app's own: after macOS holds the item back,
  the quiet reads only check it is there until the owner asks.
- The pace, runway and selection figures, the TUI and every other provider
  are not ported.

